# gdiplus: More optimizations for SOFTWARE_GdipFillPathAntialiased
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12796 state=opened
# * Perform alpha calculation and premultiplication in one pass.

* When supported, use SSE2 intrinsics to perform the above operation.

* When we are drawing (rendering?) to a non-image graphics context, write pixels directly to the DIB section that `alpha_blend_pixels_hrgn`/`alpha_blend_hdc_pixels` end up creating. This avoids reallocating another bitmap buffer and an additional memcpy.
